# `15-11`: build-time config for `npm run build:ux-gate` (`vite build --mode ux-gate`), read by
# `ux-gate/playwright.config.ts`'s own `webServer` step. Committed like `.env.production` is (see
# that file's own header, and `.gitignore`'s matching exception below) - none of these are secrets,
# they are localhost placeholders that exist only so this gate's own preview server never makes a
# same-origin call to a real deployment.
#
# All three point at `http://127.0.0.1:4173` - the exact origin `playwright.config.ts` serves the
# built app from - so every request `ux-gate/fixtures/apiStubs.ts`/`hubMock.ts` intercepts is
# same-origin and needs no CORS headers of its own. Pointing this at the real `.env.production`
# origin instead was considered and rejected for exactly that reason (`playwright.config.ts`'s own
# doc comment has the detail) - `.env.production` is not reused directly here.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4173
VITE_KEYCLOAK_AUTHORITY=http://127.0.0.1:4173/realms/ago-chat-ux-gate
VITE_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=ago-console-ux-gate
